[s0l0!-header][h1]Using Object Initializers [/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

Spaces and line breaks are not important. An object definition can span multiple lines.[code format="js" ]var John = {
  name: "John",
  age: 25
};
var James = {
  name: "James",
  age: 21
};[/code]
No matter how the object is created, the syntax for accessing the properties and methods does not change.[code format="js" codeId="691"]document.write(John.age);
[/code]
[note]Don't forget about the second accessing syntax: John['age'].[/note]

